<!-- AML Pipeline -->
<article class="case-study reveal" id="aml-pipeline">
  <div class="case-study-header">
    <span class="project-card-tier">Tier 1 Â· AI + Graph Systems Â· Sep 2025</span>
    <h2 class="case-study-title">Anti-Money Laundering Neural Pipeline</h2>
    <p class="case-study-meta">National CyberShield Hackathon Â· MANIT Bhopal Â· Team NITDominars</p>
  </div>
  <div class="case-section"><h3>Problem</h3><p>Traditional rule-based AML systems produce excessive false positives and cannot detect complex multi-layered transaction laundering patterns that span networks of shell accounts.</p></div>
  <div class="case-section"><h3>Architecture</h3>
    <div class="arch-diagram" style="position:relative;">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 800 80" style="width:100%;height:auto;" role="img" aria-label="AML Pipeline architecture">
        <defs><marker id="arrowhead" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="6" refX="8" refY="3" orient="auto"><polygon points="0 0, 8 3, 0 6" fill="var(--accent-cyan)" opacity="0.6"/></marker></defs>
        <g class="arch-svg-node" data-tip="Raw transaction data ingestion"><rect x="0" y="25" width="100" height="30" rx="6" fill="rgba(59,130,246,0.1)" stroke="var(--accent-blue)" stroke-opacity="0.4"/><text x="50" y="44" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--accent-cyan)" font-size="10" font-family="var(--font-mono)">Transactions</text></g>
        <line x1="102" y1="40" x2="128" y2="40" stroke="var(--text-muted)" stroke-opacity="0.4" marker-end="url(#arrowhead)"/>
        <g class="arch-svg-node" data-tip="2-layer GAT with 3 attention heads"><rect x="130" y="25" width="100" height="30" rx="6" fill="rgba(139,92,246,0.1)" stroke="var(--accent-purple)" stroke-opacity="0.4"/><text x="180" y="44" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--accent-cyan)" font-size="10" font-family="var(--font-mono)">GAT Model</text></g>
        <line x1="232" y1="40" x2="258" y2="40" stroke="var(--text-muted)" stroke-opacity="0.4" marker-end="url(#arrowhead)"/>
        <g class="arch-svg-node" data-tip="MLP with batch norm + dropout 0.4"><rect x="260" y="25" width="100" height="30" rx="6" fill="rgba(59,130,246,0.1)" stroke="var(--accent-blue)" stroke-opacity="0.4"/><text x="310" y="44" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--accent-cyan)" font-size="10" font-family="var(--font-mono)">MLP Classifier</text></g>
        <line x1="362" y1="40" x2="388" y2="40" stroke="var(--text-muted)" stroke-opacity="0.4" marker-end="url(#arrowhead)"/>
        <g class="arch-svg-node" data-tip="Personalized PageRank Î±=0.85"><rect x="390" y="25" width="100" height="30" rx="6" fill="rgba(139,92,246,0.1)" stroke="var(--accent-purple)" stroke-opacity="0.4"/><text x="440" y="44" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--accent-cyan)" font-size="10" font-family="var(--font-mono)">PageRank</text></g>
        <line x1="492" y1="40" x2="518" y2="40" stroke="var(--text-muted)" stroke-opacity="0.4" marker-end="url(#arrowhead)"/>
        <g class="arch-svg-node" data-tip="Cycle detection + community analysis"><rect x="520" y="25" width="120" height="30" rx="6" fill="rgba(6,182,212,0.1)" stroke="var(--accent-cyan)" stroke-opacity="0.4"/><text x="580" y="44" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--accent-cyan)" font-size="10" font-family="var(--font-mono)">Cycle Detection</text></g>
        <line x1="642" y1="40" x2="668" y2="40" stroke="var(--text-muted)" stroke-opacity="0.4" marker-end="url(#arrowhead)"/>
        <g class="arch-svg-node" data-tip="Investigation dashboard with case summaries"><rect x="670" y="25" width="120" height="30" rx="6" fill="rgba(16,185,129,0.1)" stroke="var(--accent-green)" stroke-opacity="0.4"/><text x="730" y="44" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--accent-cyan)" font-size="10" font-family="var(--font-mono)">Investigation GUI</text></g>
        <!-- Animated data packet -->
        <circle r="3" fill="var(--accent-blue)"><animateMotion dur="4s" repeatCount="indefinite" path="M50,40 L180,40 L310,40 L440,40 L580,40 L730,40" /></circle>
      </svg>
    </div>
    <p>Phase 1: Custom 2-layer Graph Attention Network with 3 attention heads and 96 hidden dimensions. Consumes 240-dimensional consolidated embeddings (source + destination + transaction features). MLP classifier with batch normalization and 0.4 dropout.</p>
    <p>Phase 2: Suspicious nodes trigger automated 2-hop and 3-hop neighborhood expansions. Personalized PageRank (Î±=0.85) propagates suspicion scores. Deterministic cycle calculations and community detection identify structural laundering loops.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="case-section"><h3>Scale</h3>
    <div class="case-metrics">
      <div class="metric"><div class="metric-value">56K+</div><div class="metric-label">Transactions</div></div>
      <div class="metric"><div class="metric-value">77K+</div><div class="metric-label">Graph Nodes</div></div>
      <div class="metric"><div class="metric-value">98.91%</div><div class="metric-label">Accuracy</div></div>
      <div class="metric"><div class="metric-value">99.81%</div><div class="metric-label">AUC-ROC</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="case-section"><h3>Technologies</h3>
    <div class="project-card-tags"><span class="tag">PyTorch</span><span class="tag">Graph Attention Networks</span><span class="tag">Neo4j</span><span class="tag">FastAPI</span><span class="tag">PageRank</span><span class="tag">Community Detection</span></div>
  </div>
  <div class="case-section"><h3>Lessons Learned</h3><p>Graph neural networks excel at detecting relational fraud patterns that tabular models miss. Personalized PageRank is remarkably effective for propagating suspicion through transaction networks. The combination of ML detection + graph investigation creates a system greater than the sum of its parts.</p></div>
</article>

